WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
A wedding seating plan: three tables, thirty guests.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.600
Who sits with whom?

3
00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:16.350
Friends together, strangers apart: you are already clustering.

4
00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:24.010
Clustering: what is tightly linked goes in one group, with few links between groups.

5
00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:29.410
You need not know who anyone is, only who is linked to whom.

6
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.022
On a chip, millions of cells are wired into one network.

7
00:00:42.022 --> 00:00:46.689
Cells in one group sit together, so their wires are short;

8
00:00:46.689 --> 00:00:51.089
wires between groups are long, slow and costly.

9
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:55.980
The course's five friends: thicker line, closer friends.

10
00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:00.380
Split them in two; the friendship cut is the cut.

11
00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:08.839
ABC | DE cuts only 3; AE | BCD cuts 12.

12
00:01:08.839 --> 00:01:14.083
Five people into two groups: 15 ways, easy to try them all.

13
00:01:14.083 --> 00:01:18.683
A hundred people? The count has 30 digits.

14
00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:25.160
Trying them one by one never ends. So we need algorithms.

15
00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:30.160
This course's eight modules are eight answers.

16
00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:35.160
They fall into a few families.

17
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:50.189
First: score every pair, then merge the closest, pair by pair (M02–M04).

18
00:01:50.189 --> 00:01:57.878
Second: let groups emerge, by label propagation or spectral methods (M05–M06).

19
00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:06.670
Third: improve a grouping by swapping pairs or moving one at a time (M07–M08).

20
00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:13.248
The last module aims for speed: make the slowest path fast (M09).

21
00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:19.560
Eight modules, one problem.

22
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:27.500
Clustering is not one algorithm but one question:

23
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:34.500
how do we group things so the links stay inside?

24
00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:40.500
Each module gives one answer.

25
00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:47.500
It starts with scoring a pair.

26
00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:56.600
Start with Module 02.
